            <ArticleTitle>Cardiac manifestations in mucopolysaccharoidosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>196-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ihj.2015.11.030</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0019-4832(15)00888-3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Through this case, we want to highlight, that in patients with mucopolysaccharoidosis (MPS), coronary arteries need to be screened in patients with LV dysfunction. Further, CT scan may not be a good modality and newer diagnostic modalities like IVUS must be offered to delineate concentric obstruction. Also, meticulous screening for hypertension must be carried out in all MPS patients.</AbstractText>
